    "https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000A6": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty, Term Track, Assistant Professor in Philosophy, School of Social Sciences (SOSS)(July 2027) (260000A6)",
      "description": "Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Term Track, Assistant Professor in Philosophy, School of Social Sciences (SOSS)(July 2027) (260000A6) Go to the main content section. You are here Faculty Recruitment Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Term Track, Assistant Professor in Philosophy, School of Social Sciences (SOSS)(July 2027) (260000A6) Job Description Full-Time Faculty, Term Track, Assistant Professor in Philosophy, School of Social Sciences (SOSS)(July 2027) - ( 260000A6 ) Description Full-Time Faculty, Assistant Professor in Philosophy, School of Social Sciences (SOSS) The School of Social Sciences, Singapore Management University, invites applications for two positions at the Assistant Professor rank (education track). Candidates must have expertise and research interests in either moral philosophy, political philosophy, social philosophy, or comparative philosophy. Candidates must also be able to teach an introductory course in critical thinking. The ability to teach introductory ethics is also highly desirable. These positions require a doctorate in Philosophy and teaching experience at the tertiary level. We are seeking candidates with demonstrated excellent teaching ability, as well as a good scholarly research record. Education track faculty teach six course sections per academic year, which is approximately nine hours of teaching per week for each semester. Course sections are capped at no more than 48 students. In addition to teaching, education track faculty are also expected to engage in research and perform internal service activities such as curriculum design and review. Singapore Management University is a research university committed to a multidisciplinary and integrated curriculum. Salary and benefits, such as a housing allowance, and research support, are highly competitive. The application package must be submitted by November 1, 2026 electronically via Careers@SMU portal. Please include: 1. A cover letter describing research and teaching interests and approaches, and outlining the candidate’s fit to the job specification. 2. Up-to-date CV (including teaching experience and a list of three referees). 3. Writing samples (maximum 2). 4. A teaching statement and a research statement (1-2 pages each). 5. Evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., teaching evaluations or syllabi). Only shortlisted candidates will be notified for interviews. All hires are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. The successful candidates will be expected to start at Singapore Management University in July 2027. Applicants should arrange for three confidential letters of recommendation to be sent directly to: The Dean’s Office, School of Social Sciences Further information about the University and the School can be found at https://socsc.smu.edu.sg/ For queries, please email Professor Tan Sor Hoon , Area Coordinator for Philosophy in the School of Social Sciences. Qualifications These positions require a doctorate in Philosophy and teaching experience at the tertiary level. Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : School of Social Sciences Job Posting : 22-Sep-2026, 11:17:07 PM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000AB": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty, Term Track, Finance (260000AB)",
      "description": "Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Term Track, Finance (260000AB) Go to the main content section. You are here Faculty Recruitment Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Term Track, Finance (260000AB) Job Description Full-Time Faculty, Term Track, Finance - ( 260000AB ) Description TERM TRACK POSITION FINANCE LEE KONG CHIAN SCHOOL OF BUSINESS SINGAPORE MANAGEMENT UNIVERSITY Full-Time Faculty, Term Track, Finance The Lee Kong Chian School of Business at the Singapore Management University (SMU) is a dynamic Asian business school with over 100 full-time faculty and about 5,500 students. AACSB, EQUIS and AMBA accredited, the School offers undergraduate, master's (including MBA and EMBA) and doctoral programmes. In the Financial Times Research Insights Ranking 2025, LKCSB was ranked 23rd globally and 3rd in Asia for overall research impact, and 6th worldwide on the ranking's teaching-case measure. Applicants are cordially invited for a full-time faculty position (Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Practice/Education) in the area of Finance at the Lee Kong Chian School of Business, Singapore Management University (SMU). Practice-track and Education-track faculty members (term track) at SMU are excellent educators who create impact through their teaching, research, and engagement with the industry. Finance Area welcome applications from candidates who have good teaching and research records in finance area. For more information about the Finance group at SMU Lee Kong Chian School of Business, visit https://business.smu.edu.sg/business/disciplines/finance/welcome . For information about Singapore, visit https://www.edb.gov.sg/en/why-singapore/a-great-place-to-live.html . English is the primary language used for education, commerce, and daily life in Singapore. Application procedure and deadline: 31 March 2027 Candidates should be prepared to submit a full application consisting of: (1) a personal statement covering their industry experience, teaching and research activities, (2) a CV, (3) three samples of research, (4) evidence of teaching ability, and (5) three letters of reference. All application materials should be submitted using the following link: Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Term Track, Finance (260000AB) with the subject heading “Practice/Education Track Application” to the attention of Associate Professor of Finance Dashan Huang via e-mail to financecv@smu.edu.sg . Qualifications Candidates must have an earned PhD in a relevant field relevant to Finance. Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : Quantitative Finance Job Posting : 17-Sep-2026, 3:23:46 AM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000A9": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Finance (260000A9)",
      "description": "Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Finance (260000A9) Go to the main content section. You are here Faculty Recruitment Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Finance (260000A9) Job Description Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Finance - ( 260000A9 ) Description FULL-TIME FACULTY POSITIONS IN FINANCE LEE KONG CHIAN SCHOOL OF BUSINESS SINGAPORE MANAGEMENT UNIVERSITY DESCRIPTION Assistant, Associate, and Full Professors of Finance Singapore Management University (SMU) invites applications for finance tenure-track and tenured positions at all levels and in all areas of scholarship. Applications in digital, sustainable, entrepreneurial, and real estate finance are particularly encouraged. LKCSB has a particular focus on high-impact research. In the Financial Times Research Insights Ranking 2025, LKCSB was ranked 23rd globally and 3rd in Asia for overall research impact, and 6th worldwide on the ranking's teaching-case measure. Therefore, research with significant (potential) impact on industry or society is particularly welcome. FULL PROFESSOR/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR : Ph.D. and established track record of high-quality research with evidence of sustained scholarship and publications in top-tier finance journals. Candidates are expected to mentor junior faculty members in research and should have effective teaching at both the undergraduate and postgraduate levels. ASSISTANT PROFESSOR : Ph.D. in hand or very close to completion. Candidates are expected to demonstrate potential for high quality research. ABOUT LEE KONG CHIAN SCHOOL OF BUSINESS AND FINANCE GROUP AT SMU : Lee Kong Chian School of Business (LKCSB) at Singapore Management University is a dynamic business school with more than 5,000 students and over a hundred full-time faculty members. Triple-accredited by AACSB, EQUIS and AMBA, the school offers a full suite of undergraduate, master’s (including the MBA) and doctoral programmes. Faculty members in the Finance group at LKCSB received their doctorates from leading research universities and regularly publish in all top-tier finance journals. In the Dallas finance research rankings, based on publications in the Journal of Finance , Journal of Financial Economics , Review of Financial Studies and Management Science for the 2023-2026 period, LKCSB was ranked 38th worldwide, as of September 2026. SMU subscribes to all major financial databases and provides generous research funds to support conference travel and other research activities. The finance group hosts an annual summer research camp, an active research seminar series, and visits by distinguished finance scholars. The finance group also has a PhD program with high quality students and good placements. For more information about the Finance group at SMU Lee Kong Chian School of Business, visit https://business.smu.edu.sg/business/disciplines/finance/welcome . For information about Singapore, visit https://www.edb.gov.sg/en/why-singapore/a-great-place-to-live.html . English is the primary language used for education, commerce, and daily life in Singapore. APPLICATION PROCEDURE AND DEADLINE : 15 November 2026 Applicants should submit their application package comprising a cover letter, CV, recent publications or working papers, teaching and research statements, and teaching evaluations via the following link : Job Description - Full-time Faculty, Tenure Track, Finance - 260000A9 In addition, three letters of recommendation should be sent via e-mail to financecv@smu.edu.sg . Please address your application to Prof Dashan Huang, Recruiting Chair and Associate Professor of Finance. Shortlisted applicants will be contacted for interviews. The first-round interviews will be conducted virtually via ZOOM before the 2027 AFA meeting. Singaporeans selected for tenure-track Assistant Professor positions may be considered for the Singapore Teaching and Academic Research Talent (START) Inauguration Grant.  Details on the grant application procedure may be found here: https://www.smu.edu.sg/moe-start/inauguration-grant Qualifications Candidates must have an earned PhD in a field relevant to Finance. Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : Finance Job Posting : 17-Sep-2026, 3:23:17 AM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=26000015": {
      "title": "SCIS Full-Time Faculty, Associate Professor on Tenure Track",
      "description": "Job Description - SCIS Full-Time Faculty, Associate Professor on Tenure Track (26000015) Go to the main content section. You are here Faculty Recruitment Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - SCIS Full-Time Faculty, Associate Professor on Tenure Track (26000015) Job Description SCIS Full-Time Faculty, Associate Professor on Tenure Track - ( 26000015 ) Description Tenure Track faculty position in Computer Science The School of Computing and Information Systems (SCIS) at the Singapore Management University (SMU) has one tenure track Associate Professor position, in the discipline of Computer Science & Engineering. We strategically hire to build critical mass and innovative capability in our core research areas and integrative research domains. In particular, we are keen to expand our faculty expertise in AI Governance (Privacy, Security, Safety, Ethics), AI in Cybersecurity, Embodied AI, Quantum Computing, Smart Financial Technology and Green Computing. OUR CORE RESEARCH AREAS Artificial Intelligence & Data Science Data Management & Mining , including databases; data mining; natural language processing; data visualisation and analytics; recommender systems; social sensing and activation. Decision Making & Optimization , including large-scale optimization and meta-heuristics; economic paradigms (game theory, mechanism design, electronic markets); agent modeling and simulation; agent planning, scheduling and decision support; agent learning and adaptation; reinforcement learning and inverse reinforcement learning. Machine Learning & Intelligence , including machine learning and adaptation; deep learning; computer vision; machine intelligence; explainable AI; cognitive/brain-inspired computing; human-centric AI; intelligent assistants; intelligence augmentation; human-in-the-loop AI. Human-Machine Collaborative System Embodied & Pervasive Systems, including sensing & sensor information processing; IoT and embedded systems; embodied AI and robotics systems; mobile and pervasive systems; context-aware and edge computing platform. Multimedia Systems , including generative media; social media; multimedia search; computer graphics; augmented reality; virtual reality. Human-Computer Interaction , including accessibility; human-AI interaction; human-robot interaction; information visualization; collaboration systems; wearable computing. Information Systems & Technology Software Engineering , including AI for SE; SE for AI; software analytics; formal methods; software testing; software maintenance & evolution; human-aspects in SE; engineering IoT, Cyber-Physical Systems & drones; sustainable SE. Cybersecurity , including decentralised/distributed trusted systems; biometrics; computer forensics; data, media content and related applications security and privacy; software and system security; information security and usability; information security economics and risk analysis, modeling & metrics. Information Systems Management , including economics of IT and management science; empirical methods, econometrics, and policy analytics; sharing economy and IT platforms; digitalisation and process transformation; fintech; marketing and healthcare IT; information security, technology innovation and IT impacts; interdisciplinary studies across the core areas. OUR INTEGRATIVE RESEARCH DOMAINS Learning & Work Urban & Sustainability Health & Wellbeing Safety, Security & Fairness While we encourage and nurture applied research addressing real-world problems, we simultaneously cultivate and value big ideas, and research that is intellectually deep and thought provoking. Our faculty target their academic output primarily in the most-selective, academically prestigious venues. We want our faculty striving to create research outputs that advance thinking and scholarship in the core research areas, and also seeking real-world impact in the integrative research domains in “the world of business”. We offer extremely attractive salary and benefits that are usually superior to international competitive benchmarks. ABOUT THE SMU SCHOOL OF COMPUTING AND INFORMATION SYSTEMS A premier university in Asia, the Singapore Management University (SMU) is internationally recognised for its world-class research and distinguished teaching. Established in 2000, SMU’s mission is to generate leading-edge research with global impact and produce broad-based, creative and entrepreneurial leaders for the knowledge-based economy. SMU education is known for its highly interactive, collaborative and project-based approach to learning, and for its technologically enabled pedagogy of seminar-style teaching in small class sizes. The School of Computing and Information Systems (SCIS) offers an exceptionally supportive and inspirational environment for academic scholarship and research, applied R&D projects, and innovative education initiatives. We currently have around 59 tenure-track faculty members working across research areas in computer science & engineering, and information systems management. They are complemented by over 36 practice/education faculty members and lecturers who focus on teaching, translation and pedagogical research. Our Research. We are passionate about our research . We aim for excellence both in fundamental contribution to academic knowledge, as well as in creating technology with practical impact. Real-world industry sectors provide SCIS with a testbed and laboratory for experimentation, as well as a fertile breeding ground for new ideas. Our faculty and students apply their research results to solve real problems in a variety of industry settings and to create IT applications and systems. At the same time, our faculty actively publish in top-quality Computer Science and Management Science conferences and journals. On our faculty are several world-class scholars and rising stars in their respective disciplines. We are committed to supporting the development of our faculty. Besides start-up support and career mentoring for junior faculty, their Ph.D. students are funded by the school rather than paid from their research grants. SCIS faculty members are encouraged to collaborate on innovative research projects and also on integrative and interdisciplinary projects. SMU as well as Singapore government agencies, such as the National Research Foundation, provide generous support for high-quality research proposals. A noteworthy example of our funded research is the Center for Research on Intelligent Software Engineering which conducts applied and fundamental research in the intersection of software engineering, artificial intelligence and cybersecurity.  In the area of Cybersecurity, SCIS has a Centre on Security, Mobile Applications and Cryptography that conducts research into mobile device, cloud, and platform security. Our Education. SCIS has more than 100 students enrolled in the Ph.D. in Information Systems and Ph.D. in Computer Science programmes. Ph.D. students can specialized in any of our computer science research areas, or in the Information Systems & Management research area. Our Doctor of Engineering (EngD) programme , a Professional Doctoral Degree, aims to train students to become IT leaders with deep technical expertise for innovating, designing and managing complex IT systems. SCIS also offers Master of IT in Business , a professionally oriented coursework programme, which has more than 400 active students. The programme supports a Financial Technology & Analytics track focusing on FinTech and the integration of Technology & Operations in Banking, an Analytics track focusing on applied analytics for business, consumer and social insights, an an Artificial Intelligence (AI) track that emphasises building AI-enabled business applications, as well as a Digital Transformation track that equips students to strategise and execute digital transformation in complex organisations. Additionally, we have approximately 1,800 undergraduate students in our B.Sc. (Computer Science) , B.Sc. (Information Systems) , B.Sc. (Computing & Law) and B.Sc. (Software Engineering ) programmes. The programmes have been remarkably successful in demonstrating educational innovations and creating a culture of learning, establishing external linkages and partnerships with industry, government and the social sector, and in job placement outcomes. We have an entrepreneurial student body, and many SCIS undergraduates have gone on to create or participate in start-ups . Qualifications We are continuously on the lookout for outstanding faculty candidates at all levels: Senior Postdocs looking for a faculty position Ph.D. holders who are currently in industry but want to return to faculty and research work Mid-career faculty Tenure track faculty must have Ph.D. qualification in a relevant discipline (such as Computer Science, Computer Engineering and Information Technology) along with an outstanding research record. Interested candidates are invited to submit a cover letter (indicating which of the above Core Research Areas your research interest belongs to), curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, three recommendation letters, and three samples of published work to: SCIS Faculty Recruitment Singapore Management University School of Computing and Information Systems (SCIS) 80 Stamford Road Singapore 178902 Republic of Singapore E-mail: sciscv@smu.edu.sg Website: scis.smu.edu.sg Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : School of Computing and Information Systems Job Posting : 10-Sep-2026, 3:33:11 AM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600007L": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Operations Management (2600007L)",
      "description": "Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Operations Management (2600007L) Go to the main content section. You are here Faculty Recruitment Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Operations Management (2600007L) Job Description Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Operations Management - ( 2600007L ) Description TENURED / TENURE-TRACK FACULTY POSITIONS IN OPERATIONS MANAGEMENT The Lee Kong Chian School of Business (LKCSB) at Singapore Management University (SMU) invites applications for multiple tenured/tenure-track faculty positions in Operations Management (OM) at all ranks. A Ph.D. (or near completion in the case of junior Assistant rank) in OM or a closely related field is required. While the positions are open for any candidate with research interests in broad domains of OM, those specializing in analytics (AI, machine learning), entrepreneurship, or sustainability are specifically encouraged to apply. LKCSB has a particular focus on high-impact research. In the recent FT Research Impact ranking, LKCSB was ranked 3rd in Asia and 23rd globally. Therefore, research with high academic impact and/or with significant (potential) impact on industry or society is particularly welcome. LKCSB is a vibrant and culturally diverse business school, located in the heart of downtown Singapore, with approximately 5,500 students and over 130 full-time faculty members. The school offers a wide array of undergraduate and postgraduate programs, including Ph.D, MBA, EMBA, MSc, DBA, as well as executive education . The OM group at LKCSB consists of 24 faculty members with diverse research expertise with strong publication record. LKCSB provides internationally competitive remuneration, generous research support and conference funding. International faculty are offered housing and schooling subsidy as well as relocation assistance. The teaching load for pre-tenure faculty is 2 courses per academic year during their initial four-year contract, 3 courses per academic year during the second three-year contract (if renewed) and after tenure. Tenured faculty members with exceptional research performance are also eligible for reduced teaching loads. Applications must be submitted through the following link: Job Description - Full-time Faculty, Tenure Track, Operations Management - 2600007L Applicants should include a full CV, up to three selected publications/working papers, and a cover letter. Applicants for pre-tenure positions should also include research and teaching statements. Shortlisted candidates will be asked to provide three reference letters (referees will be requested to send directly to the school). Candidates who start their application by 23:59 PM on October 11, 2026 (Singapore time, UTC/GMT +8) with an up-to-date CV will be considered for online interviews ahead of the INFORMS Annual Meeting. The deadline for completion of all submissions is 23:59 PM on November 8, 2026 (Singapore time, UTC/GMT +8). Late applications will be accepted, but may not receive full consideration. Qualifications Candidates must have an earned PhD in a field relevant to Operations Management. Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : Operations Management Job Posting : 17-Aug-2026, 3:26:55 AM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600007K": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty, Tenure or Tenured Track Faculty Position in Accounting (2600007K)",
      "description": "Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure or Tenured Track Faculty Position in Accounting (2600007K) Go to the main content section. You are here Faculty Recruitment Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure or Tenured Track Faculty Position in Accounting (2600007K) Job Description Full-Time Faculty, Tenure or Tenured Track Faculty Position in Accounting - ( 2600007K ) Description TENURE TRACK OR TENURED (OPEN RANK) FACULTY POSITIONS IN ACCOUNTING The School of Accountancy (SOA) at Singapore Management University (SMU) invites applications for openings of tenure track or tenured faculty positions in accounting with employment commencing 1 July 2027. ABOUT SCHOOL OF ACCOUNTANCY The School of Accountancy has built an outstanding reputation for its significant contributions to accounting research and high-quality accounting education; it is currently ranked amongst the top ten accounting schools in the world (Brigham Young University rankings) and counts world-class scholars and business leaders as part of its team. The School’s research is both academic-driven and practice oriented; it offers holistic education underpinning its suite of distinctive programmes - the Bachelor of Accountancy (BAcc), the Master of Professional Accounting (MPA), the Master of Science in Accounting (MSA) (Data & Analytics) and the PhD in Accounting – as well as coveted thought leadership and broad collaboration with businesses and society. Please visit https://accountancy.smu.edu.sg/ for more information on the School. REMUNERATION AND BENEFITS SMU offers internationally competitive remuneration and assistance to international faculty to help them take up their appointments in Singapore. Details of remuneration and compensation are provided to candidates during the recruitment process, however the following may provide a guide. •    9-month academic year •    research support •    medical insurance •    fund contributions, or service gratuity (for international faculty) •    housing subsidy (for international faculty) •    schooling subsidy (for children of international faculty) •    relocation assistance and support (for international faculty) •    faculty may take advantage of extramural professional or consulting opportunities Qualifications REQUIREMENTS Applicants for the position must have a PhD in Accounting or related fields, or anticipate to obtain the PhD degree before joining. SOA is looking for individuals who demonstrate significant achievements or potential in scholarly research as well as ability and promise in teaching excellence in both undergraduate and postgraduate courses.  To be considered for a rank above Assistant Professor, an excellent record of scholarly research activities and teaching that is consistent with a senior-level faculty appointment is required. APPLICATION DEADLINE Review of applications is ongoing, with a deadline of 15 November 2026 for applicants of assistant professor positions. PRESIDENTIAL EARLY CAREER PROFESSOR SMU is now inviting applications for the Presidential Early Career Professorship (SMU-PEP) – a prestigious tenure-track position for outstanding early-career scholars. The scheme offers a generous sign-on bonus, start-up research funding, dedicated mentorship, and opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. It is open to candidates from all disciplines. Applicants for the position should have earned a PhD (or equivalent) within the past 6 years (or are awaiting formal graduation), with an excellent research track record and demonstrated potential for impactful, interdisciplinary contributions. More information is available at https://careers.smu.edu.sg/presidential-early-career-professorship. Applications are now open and will close on 15 October 2026 for the 2027 intake. SINGAPORE TEACHING AND ACADEMIC RESEARCH TALENT (START) INAUGURATION GRANT Singaporeans selected for tenure track faculty positions may be considered for the Singapore Teaching and Academic Research Talent (START) Inauguration Grant.  Details on the grant application procedure may be found here: https://www.smu.edu.sg/moe-start/inauguration-grant. Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : School of Accountancy Job Posting : 13-Aug-2026, 11:25:00 PM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600007B": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty, Term Track, Quantitative Finance (2600007B)",
      "description": "Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Term Track, Quantitative Finance (2600007B) Go to the main content section. You are here Faculty Recruitment Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Term Track, Quantitative Finance (2600007B) Job Description Full-Time Faculty, Term Track, Quantitative Finance - ( 2600007B ) Description LECTURER & SENIOR LECTURER POSITIONS IN QUANTITATIVE FINANCE LEE KONG CHIAN SCHOOL OF BUSINESS SINGAPORE MANAGEMENT UNIVERSITY Singapore Management University’s Quantitative Finance group invites applications for Lecturer and/or Senior Lecturer (teaching-only) positions. Lecturers are required to teach 8 courses per academic year. We seek candidates with a PhD degree, or its equivalent, from a reputable university, proven teaching records, and relevant professional industry experience. The position starts on 1 January 2027 . Further information about the Quantitative Finance group can be found at https://business.smu.edu.sg/disciplines/quantitative-finance . About Singapore Management University & the Lee Kong Chian School of Business Established in 2000, Singapore Management University (SMU) is recognised for its disciplinary and multidisciplinary research that addresses issues of global relevance, impacting business, government, and society. Its distinctive education, incorporating innovative experiential learning, aims to nurture global citizens, entrepreneurs and change agents. Today, SMU is home to more than 13,000 students with over four hundred faculty members comprising eight schools. The Lee Kong Chian School of Business has over a hundred full-time faculty and more than 5,000 students. Triple-accredited by AACSB, EQUIS and AMBA, the school offers a full suite of undergraduate, master’s (including the MBA) and doctoral programmes. Successful candidates can expect excellent conditions for teaching, a collegial and supportive environment, and the experience of living and teaching in a dynamic and exciting region of the world. SMU offers an internationally competitive compensation package including relocation benefits and child education funding. General information about SMU can be found at www.smu.edu.sg . APPLICATION PROCEDURES All applications should be submitted using the following link: Job Description - Full-time Faculty, Term Track, Quantitative Finance (2600007B) A full application should be submitted by 1 st October 2026. Applications should include (1) a CV, (2) a Cover Letter, (3) a Teaching Statement, (4) Teaching Evaluations (including both numerical and narrative feedback) and (5) 3 Letter of References (to be provided directly by referees). All application materials should be uploaded as attachments under their profile via the system. (Referees may send their reference letters directly to QuantFin@smu.edu.sg addressing the application to the QF Recruiting Committee.) Qualifications Candidates must have an earned PhD in a relevant field (such as quantitative finance, mathematics, computer science, statistics, engineering, economics, information system, or a related cross disciplinary field). Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : Quantitative Finance Job Posting : 03-Aug-2026, 11:22:21 PM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=26000078": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Strategy & Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Strategy & Entrepreneurship (26000078) Go to the main content section. You are here Faculty Recruitment Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Strategy & Entrepreneurship (26000078) Job Description Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Strategy & Entrepreneurship - ( 26000078 ) Description FACULTY POSITIONS STRATEGY & ENTREPRENEURSHIP AREA LEE KONG CHIAN SCHOOL OF BUSINESS SINGAPORE MANAGEMENT UNIVERSITY Singapore Management University’s Strategy & Entrepreneurship group invites applications for multiple tenure-track faculty position across all levels (Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, and Full Professor) . We are seeking leading experts particularly in Entrepreneurship and Innovation , but also from one of the following broadly defined areas of Strategic Management, International Business, Organizational Theory (Macro), Environmental Sustainability and CSR, and Technology Management and Digitalization (including AI). We expect candidates to be conducting rigorous, impactful, and interesting research, and have top-tier publishing and research records (e.g., AMJ, AMR, ASQ, Org Sci, SMJ, etc) commensurate with the rank they are applying for. SMU offers an internationally competitive compensation and research support package including relocation benefits and child education funding. About the Strategy and Entrepreneurship Area: The Strategy and Entrepreneurship Area currently has 25+ tenure-, practice- and teaching-track faculty members from over 10 different nationalities. They conduct high-quality research published in top research journals and have extensive editorial experience. Senior faculty members include Ilya Cuypers, Gokhan Ertug, Reddi Kotha, Heli Wang, Daphne Yiu among others. General information about SMU can be found at www.smu.edu.sg and information about the Strategy & Entrepreneurship area at: https://business.smu.edu.sg/business/disciplines/strategy-and-entrepreneurship/welcome APPLICATION PROCEDURES All applications should be submitted using the following link: Job Description - Full-time Faculty, Tenure Track, Strategy & Entrepreneurship (26000078) Candidates should submit a full application by 15 September 2026 consisting of: (1) a letter with their research and teaching statement, (2) a CV, (3) three samples of research, (4) evidence of teaching ability, and (5) three letters of reference. Candidates can upload the reference letters or a list of reference contacts : as attachments under their profile via the system or send the reference letters directly to managementcv@smu.edu.sg Full Professors and established Associate Professors may send just a cover letter and CV to managementcv@smu.edu.sg and liangchen@smu.edu.sg with the subject heading “ Tenure-track Application” , and will be considered on an ongoing-basis until the position is filled. Our senior faculty members are available for conversations at the AOM and SMS conferences. Contact liangchen@smu.edu.sg for more details. #LI-DNI Qualifications Candidates must have an earned PhD in a field relevant to Strategy and Entrepreneurship. Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : Strategy & Entrepreneurship Job Posting : 27-Jul-2026, 11:24:45 PM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=26000075": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Organisational Behaviour & Human Resources",
      "description": "Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Organisational Behaviour & Human Resources (26000075) Go to the main content section. You are here Faculty Recruitment Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Organisational Behaviour & Human Resources (26000075) Job Description Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Organisational Behaviour & Human Resources - ( 26000075 ) Description FACULTY POSITIONS IN OBHR LEE KONG CHIAN SCHOOL OF BUSINESS SINGAPORE MANAGEMENT UNIVERSITY Singapore Management University’s Organisational Behaviour and Human Resources (OBHR) group invites applications for tenure-track faculty positions with a preference for applicants at the Assistant Professor level. We seek candidates who conduct rigorous, impactful, and theoretically significant research in organisational behaviour and/or human resources. Candidates should have a strong research pipeline, and a record of, or clear potential for publishing in leading scholarly journals commensurate with their career stage. Applicants should also demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching. Entry-level candidates should be near completion of, or have recently completed, a PhD in organisational behaviour, human resources, or a related discipline. Application review will begin immediately, with full consideration given to applications received by 5:00 p.m. Singapore time on 21 August 2026 . About the Organisational Behaviour and Human Resources Area The OBHR group comprises twenty-five faculty members. It is one of the most productive groups of OBHR researchers in Asia, and is recognized for its strong research culture and collegial environment. Our faculty regularly publish in top-tier OBHR journals and serve as Associate Editors and on the editorial boards of these journals. The OBHR group supports a thriving PhD programme and fosters a collaborative culture that values both rigorous scholarship and practical impact. Additional information about the Organisational Behaviour and Human Resources group can be found at https://business.smu.edu.sg/business/disciplines/organisational-behaviour-and-human-resources/welcome . About SMU and the Lee Kong Chian School of Business Singapore Management University (SMU) is a premier research university committed to rigorous, interdisciplinary work with real-world relevance. Located in the heart of Singapore’s central business district, SMU offers a dynamic, globally oriented environment for both research and teaching. The Lee Kong Chian School of Business (LKCSB) has over 100 full-time faculty members and approximately 5,500 students. It consistently ranks among the top business schools worldwide, including in Financial Times (FT) and QS global rankings, and holds triple-crown accreditation from AACSB, EQUIS, and AMBA. In the FT Research Insights Ranking 2025, LKCSB ranked 3rd in Asia and 23rd globally. LKCSB offers globally competitive compensation, substantial research support (e.g., research funding, data access, and research assistant support), and a low teaching load to facilitate high-quality scholarship. Living in Singapore: Singapore is a vibrant city-state, offering world-class amenities, excellent healthcare, and a safe environment. Its efficient public transport system and abundant greenery make it an attractive city to live and work. Residents enjoy diverse leisure options, from parks, nature trails, beaches, and sports facilities to theatres, museums, and galleries. Singapore is also very family-friendly, with excellent private and public schools. Singapore’s innovation-driven economy has transformed it into one of the world’s leading business and financial hubs. With world-class connectivity through Changi International Airport, Singapore offers an ideal base for both regional and international travel. The city’s multicultural society, shaped by Chinese, Malay, Indian, and Eurasian communities, supports a rich tapestry of festivals, traditions, and cuisines. Food enthusiasts can explore acclaimed restaurants and local hawker centres—the city is a culinary delight! Procedures for a pplicants at the Assistant Professor level: All applications should be submitted through our online portal under the Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, OBHR (26000075) Applications should include: a letter with research and teaching statements a curriculum vitae three samples of research evidence of teaching effectiveness three letters of reference Reference letters can be uploaded as attachments under applicants’ profile via the online portal OR sent directly to obhrcv@smu.edu.sg addressing the application to the OBHR Recruiting Committee. The search is primarily focused on the Assistant Professor level, although outstanding candidates at the Associate Professor or Full Professor level could also be considered. Full Professors and Associate Professors may send only a cover letter and a curriculum vitae to obhrcv@smu.edu.sg with the subject heading “Tenured Application”; applications will be considered on an ongoing-basis. #LI-DNI Qualifications Candidates must have an earned PhD in a field relevant to Organisational Behaviour and Human Resources. Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : Organisational Behaviour & Human Resources Job Posting : 22-Jul-2026, 8:05:59 PM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600006E": {
      "title": "SMU Presidential Early Career Professorship (2600006E)",
      "description": "Job Description - SMU Presidential Early Career Professorship (2600006E) Go to the main content section. You are here Faculty Recruitment Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - SMU Presidential Early Career Professorship (2600006E) Job Description SMU Presidential Early Career Professorship - ( 2600006E ) Description Join Singapore Management University As A Presidential Early Career Professor Tenure-Track Assistant Or Associate Professor Positions Singapore Management University (SMU), a research-intensive university with recognised strengths in management, computing, law, economics, and social sciences, invites outstanding scholars to join us as tenure-track Assistant Professor or Associate Professor under the University's Presidential Early Career Professorship (SMU-PEP) Scheme . Following the successful inaugural round of the SMU-PEP Scheme in 2025, SMU is pleased to open its second call for applications from scholars whose research aligns with SMU’s strategic research priorities: · Digital Transformation · Sustainable Living · Growth in Asia. Early-career scholars from any academic discipline whose work addresses the challenges of ageing societies, sustainable cities, or resilient workforces are especially encouraged to apply. Exceptional candidates working outside these priority areas are welcome to apply. What We Offer Successful candidates will be appointed to a named (early-career) professorship and can expect: A vibrant and collegial research and teaching environment Internationally competitive compensation A generous sign-on bonus and start-up research grant Comprehensive benefits The opportunity to live and work in one of Asia’s most exciting and cosmopolitan cities Qualifications Applicants should: Hold a Ph.D. or equivalent degree, earned within six years of the application date Have postdoctoral research and teaching experience Demonstrate an excellent research track record, particularly in interdisciplinary work Show strong potential to contribute high-impact future research Application Instructions Please submit the following by 31 October 2026 : Cover letter with your research and teaching statements Curriculum vitae Three research samples Evidence of teaching effectiveness Shortlisted candidates will be notified and asked to arrange for three academic reference letters. The expected start date is 1 July 2027 , or as mutually agreed. All applications will be handled in strict confidence. Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted. At SMU, we value diversity and are committed to building an inclusive and supportive workplace for all. Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : PEP_SCHEME Job Posting : 21-Jun-2026, 8:33:33 PM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600006G": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty, Research Track Positions at the Associate or Full Professor Levels in Urban Analytics/Innovation or Urban Studies, SMU Urban Institute (2600006G)",
      "description": "Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Research Track Positions at the Associate or Full Professor Levels in Urban Analytics/Innovation or Urban Studies, SMU Urban Institute (2600006G) Go to the main content section. You are here Faculty Recruitment Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Research Track Positions at the Associate or Full Professor Levels in Urban Analytics/Innovation or Urban Studies, SMU Urban Institute (2600006G) Job Description Full-Time Faculty, Research Track Positions at the Associate or Full Professor Levels in Urban Analytics/Innovation or Urban Studies, SMU Urban Institute - ( 2600006G ) Description Full-Time Faculty, Research Track Positions at the Associate or Full Professor Levels in Urban Analytics/Innovation or Urban Studies, SMU Urban Institute The Urban Institute (UI) at Singapore Management University (SMU) invites applications for up to three full-time, non-tenurable Research Track faculty positions at the Associate or Full Professor level in Urban Analytics/Innovation or Urban Studies. These are fixed-term appointments for three years in the first instance, with the possibility of renewal. Research Track faculty at SMU are expected to pursue high-quality, impactful research, contribute to interdisciplinary scholarship, and participate in the broader academic and intellectual lives of the UI and SMU. The teaching load is one course per year, and successful applicants will have clear KPIs in terms of publishing and grant-winning. The UI is a university-level research institute dedicated to delivering impact through interdisciplinary research on Asian cities. Its vision is to advance an approach to studying and understanding the city that is human-centred, innovation-driven, and Asia-focused. Guided by four research pillars – Growth, Governance, Systems, Experiences – the UI understands the city in holistic terms, and seeks to develop the understanding and insight needed to make Asia’s cities more liveable, inclusive and resilient places. We are interested in candidates who are able to push the boundaries of urban research in areas such as, but not limited to, urban sustainability, urban systems and infrastructures (including smart cities and AI enabled urban systems), urban liveability and inequality, and/or novel approaches to urban theory development. We also welcome applicants trained in Data Science/Analytics, Computer Science, Geographical Information Systems, Informatics, Geomatics, Urban or Development Economics, Public Policy, Urban Planning, Urban Engineering (all with an urban application), or in cognate disciplinary or interdisciplinary fields with an urban focus. Candidates that can demonstrate bold interdisciplinarity in research are particularly encouraged to apply, as are those with demonstrable experience conducting research in and on cities in Asia. Prior experience working within Singapore’s higher education landscape is a bonus. Applicants should be able to: Conceptualise and execute high quality research projects, and develop grant applications on urban-related issues in Asia, broadly defined Design and deliver an undergraduate or postgraduate course on urban-related topics Participate actively in the research and educational communities at SMU, and contribute to at least one of the university’s three areas of strategic priority: Growth in Asia, Digital Transformation, and Sustainable Living Contribute to the dynamic intellectual life at UI as well as to interdisciplinary dialogue and exchange with colleagues from other Schools (such as Computing and Information Systems, Economics, Law, Business, and the Humanities and Social Sciences) Qualifications: ● Ph.D. in either a computational discipline (e.g., Data Science/Analytics/Informatics, Computer Science, Geographical Information Systems, Geomatics, Urban or Developmental Economics, Urban Planning, Engineering with an urban focus, or Building Science), or an interdisciplinary (e.g., Urban Science, Urban Studies, Development Studies, or Architecture) field ● A strong international research and publication record, including publications in leading peer-reviewed journals. ● Excellent oral and written communication and presentation skills Application procedure We invite candidates to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching statement, research statement, two samples of written work published in English to SMU Career . Applicants should also arrange for three academic references to be sent directly to urban@smu.edu.sg with the subject line: [Applicant’s Full Name] – Research Track Reference. Please note that incomplete applications slow down the recruitment process and might not be considered as a result. Additional supporting materials may be requested from shortlisted candidates during the selection process. SMU is committed to fostering diversity and cultivating an inclusive work environment. Applications from women and minorities are particularly encouraged. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to a campus visit. We envision interviews and campus visits to take place in October 2026, with the expected start date for the successful candidate being from June 2027 onwards. The deadline for applications is 4 September 2026, although the applications portal will remain open until the position is filled. Qualifications Qualifications: ● Ph.D. in either a computational discipline (e.g., Data Science/Analytics/Informatics, Computer Science, Geographical Information Systems, Geomatics, Urban or Developmental Economics, Urban Planning, Engineering with an urban focus, or Building Science), or an interdisciplinary (e.g., Urban Science, Urban Studies, Development Studies, or Architecture) field ● A strong international research and publication record, including publications in leading peer-reviewed journals. ● Excellent oral and written communication and presentation skills Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : SMU Urban Institute Job Posting : 21-Jun-2026, 7:51:54 PM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600005Y": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Marketing (2600005Y)",
      "description": "Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Marketing (2600005Y) Go to the main content section. You are here Faculty Recruitment Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Marketing (2600005Y) Job Description Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Marketing - ( 2600005Y ) Description FACULTY POSITIONS IN MARKETING (Assistant / Advanced Assistant / Associate / Full Professor - All Areas) The Marketing Area at the Lee Kong Chian School of Business, Singapore Management University (SMU), invites applications for full-time, tenure-track faculty positions. The search is open across both rank and area. We welcome candidates at all ranks (assistant, advanced assistant, associate, and full professor) and in all areas of marketing. LKCSB has a particular focus on high-impact research. Therefore, research with significant (potential) impact on industry or society is particularly welcome. Candidates should have a research and teaching record commensurate with the rank for which they are applying. Entry-level candidates should be near completion of, or have recently completed, a PhD in Marketing or a related discipline such as Psychology, Economics, Statistics, or Computer Science. Application review will begin immediately, with full consideration given to applications received by 5:00 p.m. Singapore time on 15 Jul 2026 . About the Marketing Area Join a vibrant and expanding Marketing Area recognized for its strong research culture, collegial environment, and deep industry connections. Our faculty regularly publish in leading journals such as the Journal of Marketing Research, the Journal of Marketing, the Journal of Consumer Research, Marketing Science, and Management Science, as well as top outlets in related disciplines (e.g., the Journal of Personality and Social Psychology and Psychological Science). Many of our faculty serve as co-Editors, Associate Editors, and on the editorial boards of these journals, actively shaping the field. The Marketing Area supports a thriving PhD program and fosters a collaborative atmosphere, with a state-of-the-art behavioral research lab, access to diverse field and secondary data through extensive industry partnerships, and a culture that values both rigorous scholarship and practical impact. About SMU and the Lee Kong Chian School of Business Singapore Management University (SMU) is a premier research university committed to rigorous, interdisciplinary work with real-world relevance. Located in the heart of Singapore’s downtown district, SMU offers a dynamic, globally oriented environment for both research and teaching. The Lee Kong Chian School of Business (LKCSB) has over 100 full-time faculty members and approximately 5,500 students. It consistently ranks among the top business schools worldwide, including in Financial Times and QS global rankings, and holds triple-crown accreditation from AACSB, EQUIS, and AMBA. In the FT Research Insights Ranking 2025, LKCSB is ranked 3rd in Asia and 23rd globally. We are proud to be the youngest business school in the global top 25. LKCSB offers globally competitive compensation, substantial research support (e.g., research funding, data, and RA support), and a low teaching load to facilitate high-quality scholarship. Living in Singapore: Singapore may measure just 50km by 27km, but its global impact and quality of life are immense. A vibrant city-state, it offers world-class amenities, excellent healthcare, and a safe environment, with one of the lowest crime rates globally. Its efficient public transport system (MRT, LRT, buses, taxis, and private-hire services), clean streets, and abundant greenery make it easy and pleasant to live and work in the city. Since independence, Singapore’s stable parliamentary democracy and strong, innovation-driven economy have transformed it into one of the world’s leading business and financial hubs. The city’s multicultural society, shaped by Chinese, Malay, Indian, and Eurasian communities, supports a rich tapestry of festivals, traditions, and cuisines. Residents enjoy diverse leisure options, from parks, nature trails, beaches, and sports facilities to theatres, museums, and galleries. Food enthusiasts can explore everything from acclaimed restaurants to local hawker centers, which UNESCO recognizes as part of the world’s Intangible Cultural Heritage. Singapore’s advanced infrastructure and technology, including the Smart Nation initiative, underpin high-quality public services and a sustainable urban environment. With world-class connectivity through Changi International Airport, consistently voted among the best airports globally, Singapore offers an ideal base for both regional and international travel. Application procedure All applications should be submitted through our online portal under the Job Description – Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Marketing (2600005Y) . Required materials depend on the rank applied for. Applicants at the Assistant Professor (entry) level should submit: (1) a cover letter summarizing your candidacy and specifying the desired rank (2) a detailed curriculum vitae (3) a personal statement on research and teaching (4) a job market paper or three research samples (5) evidence of teaching effectiveness, such as a teaching dossier or teaching evaluations, where available (6) three letters of reference Applicants at the Advanced Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor level should submit: (1) a detailed curriculum vitae (2) three research samples For inquiries about the position (excluding application materials submissions), please contact Professor Jin K. Han, Marketing Area, Lee Kong Chian School of Business, Singapore Management University, at jkhan@smu.edu.sg . #LI-DNI Qualifications Candidates must have an earned PhD in a field relevant to Marketing. Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : Marketing Job Posting : 08-Jun-2026, 8:17:42 PM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=26000001": {
      "title": "SCIS Full-Time Faculty, Assistant Professor on Tenure Track",
      "description": "Job Description - SCIS Full-Time Faculty, Assistant Professor on Tenure Track (26000001) Go to the main content section. You are here Faculty Recruitment Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - SCIS Full-Time Faculty, Assistant Professor on Tenure Track (26000001) Job Description SCIS Full-Time Faculty, Assistant Professor on Tenure Track - ( 26000001 ) Description Tenure Track faculty position in Computer Science The School of Computing and Information Systems (SCIS) at the Singapore Management University (SMU) has one tenure track faculty position, Assistant Professor, in the discipline of Computer Science & Engineering. We strategically hire to build critical mass and innovative capability in our core research areas and integrative research domains. In particular, we are keen to expand our faculty expertise in AI Governance (Privacy, Security, Safety, Ethics), AI in Cybersecurity, Embodied AI, Quantum Computing, Smart Financial Technology and Green Computing. OUR CORE RESEARCH AREAS · Artificial Intelligence & Data Science o Data Management & Mining, including databases; data mining; natural language processing; data visualisation and analytics; recommender systems; social sensing and activation. o Decision Making & Optimization, including large-scale optimization and meta-heuristics; economic paradigms (game theory, mechanism design, electronic markets); agent modeling and simulation; agent planning, scheduling and decision support; agent learning and adaptation; reinforcement learning and inverse reinforcement learning. o Machine Learning & Intelligence, including machine learning and adaptation; deep learning; computer vision; machine intelligence; explainable AI; cognitive/brain-inspired computing; human-centric AI; intelligent assistants; intelligence augmentation; human-in-the-loop AI. · Human-Machine Collaborative Systems o Embodied & Pervasive Systems, including sensing & sensor information processing; IoT and embedded systems; embodied AI and robotics systems; mobile and pervasive systems; context-aware and edge computing platform. o Multimedia Systems , including generative media; social media; multimedia search; computer graphics; augmented reality; virtual reality. o Human-Computer Interaction , including accessibility; human-AI interaction; human-robot interaction; information visualization; collaboration systems; wearable computing. · Information Systems & Technology o Software Engineering , including AI for SE; SE for AI; software analytics; formal methods; software testing; software maintenance & evolution; human-aspects in SE; engineering IoT, Cyber-Physical Systems & drones; sustainable SE. o Cybersecurity , including decentralised/distributed trusted systems; biometrics; computer forensics; data, media content and related applications security and privacy; software and system security; information security and usability; information security economics and risk analysis, modeling & metrics. o Information Systems Management , including economics of IT and management science; empirical methods, econometrics, and policy analytics; sharing economy and IT platforms; digitalisation and process transformation; fintech; marketing and healthcare IT; information security, technology innovation and IT impacts; interdisciplinary studies across the core areas. OUR INTEGRATIVE RESEARCH DOMAINS Learning & Work Urban & Sustainability Health & Wellbeing Safety, Security & Fairness While we encourage and nurture applied research addressing real-world problems, we simultaneously cultivate and value big ideas, and research that is intellectually deep and thought provoking. Our faculty target their academic output primarily in the most-selective, academically prestigious venues. We want our faculty striving to create research outputs that advance thinking and scholarship in the core research areas, and also seeking real-world impact in the integrative research domains in “the world of business”. We offer extremely attractive salary and benefits that are usually superior to international competitive benchmarks. ABOUT THE SMU SCHOOL OF COMPUTING AND INFORMATION SYSTEMS A premier university in Asia, the Singapore Management University (SMU) is internationally recognised for its world-class research and distinguished teaching. Established in 2000, SMU’s mission is to generate leading-edge research with global impact and produce broad-based, creative and entrepreneurial leaders for the knowledge-based economy. SMU education is known for its highly interactive, collaborative and project-based approach to learning, and for its technologically enabled pedagogy of seminar-style teaching in small class sizes. The School of Computing and Information Systems (SCIS) offers an exceptionally supportive and inspirational environment for academic scholarship and research, applied R&D projects, and innovative education initiatives. We currently have around 59 tenure-track faculty members working across research areas in computer science & engineering, and information systems management. They are complemented by over 36 practice/education faculty members and lecturers who focus on teaching, translation and pedagogical research. Our Research. We are passionate about our research . We aim for excellence both in fundamental contribution to academic knowledge, as well as in creating technology with practical impact. Real-world industry sectors provide SCIS with a testbed and laboratory for experimentation, as well as a fertile breeding ground for new ideas. Our faculty and students apply their research results to solve real problems in a variety of industry settings and to create IT applications and systems. At the same time, our faculty actively publish in top-quality Computer Science and Management Science conferences and journals. On our faculty are several world-class scholars and rising stars in their respective disciplines. We are committed to supporting the development of our faculty. Besides start-up support and career mentoring for junior faculty, their Ph.D. students are funded by the school rather than paid from their research grants. SCIS faculty members are encouraged to collaborate on innovative research projects and also on integrative and interdisciplinary projects. SMU as well as Singapore government agencies, such as the National Research Foundation, provide generous support for high-quality research proposals. A noteworthy example of our funded research is the Center for Research on Intelligent Software Engineering which conducts applied and fundamental research in the intersection of software engineering, artificial intelligence and cybersecurity.  In the area of Cybersecurity, SCIS has a Centre on Security, Mobile Applications and Cryptography that conducts research into mobile device, cloud, and platform security. Our Education. SCIS has more than 100 students enrolled in the Ph.D. in Information Systems and Ph.D. in Computer Science programmes. Ph.D. students can specialized in any of our computer science research areas, or in the Information Systems & Management research area. Our Doctor of Engineering (EngD) programme , a Professional Doctoral Degree, aims to train students to become IT leaders with deep technical expertise for innovating, designing and managing complex IT systems. SCIS also offers Master of IT in Business , a professionally oriented coursework programme, which has more than 400 active students. The programme supports a Financial Technology & Analytics track focusing on FinTech and the integration of Technology & Operations in Banking, an Analytics track focusing on applied analytics for business, consumer and social insights, an an Artificial Intelligence (AI) track that emphasises building AI-enabled business applications, as well as a Digital Transformation track that equips students to strategise and execute digital transformation in complex organisations. Additionally, we have approximately 1,800 undergraduate students in our B.Sc. (Computer Science) , B.Sc. (Information Systems) , B.Sc. (Computing & Law) and B.Sc. (Software Engineering) programmes. The programmes have been remarkably successful in demonstrating educational innovations and creating a culture of learning, establishing external linkages and partnerships with industry, government and the social sector, and in job placement outcomes. We have an entrepreneurial student body, and many SCIS undergraduates have gone on to create or participate in start-ups . Qualifications We are continuously on the lookout for outstanding faculty candidates at all levels: Fresh Ph.D. graduates Postdocs looking for a faculty position Ph.D. holders who are currently in industry but want to return to faculty and research work Mid-career or senior faculty Tenure track faculty must have Ph.D. qualification in a relevant discipline (such as Computer Science, Computer Engineering and Information Technology) along with an outstanding research record. Singaporeans selected for tenure track faculty positions may be considered for the Singapore Teaching and Academic Research Talent (START) Inauguration Grant. Details on the grant application procedure may be found here: https://www.smu.edu.sg/moe-start/inauguration-grant . Interested candidates are invited to submit a cover letter (indicating which of the above Core Research Areas your research interest belongs to), curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, three recommendation letters, and three samples of published work to: SCIS Faculty Recruitment Singapore Management University School of Computing and Information Systems (SCIS) 80 Stamford Road Singapore 178902 Republic of Singapore E-mail: sciscv@smu.edu.sg Website: scis.smu.edu.sg Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : School of Computing and Information Systems Job Posting : 06-Jan-2026, 1:33:45 AM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
    },
