    "https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=250000C4": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Marketing (250000C4)",
      "description": "Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Marketing (250000C4) Go to the main content section. You are here Faculty Recruitment Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Marketing (250000C4) Job Description Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Marketing - ( 250000C4 ) Description FACULTY POSITIONS IN MARKETING (Advanced Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - All Areas) The Marketing Area at the Lee Kong Chian School of Business, Singapore Management University (SMU), invites applications for full-time faculty positions at all non-rookie levels (advanced assistant, associate, and full professor). We welcome candidates with strong research and teaching records in all areas of marketing, including Quantitative Marketing, Marketing Strategy, and Consumer Behavior. Application review will begin immediately, with full consideration given to applications received by January 3, 2026. About the Marketing Area Join a vibrant and expanding Marketing Area recognized for its strong research culture, collegial environment, and deep industry connections. Our faculty regularly publish in leading journals such as the Journal of Marketing Research, the Journal of Marketing, the Journal of Consumer Research, Marketing Science, and Management Science, as well as top outlets in related disciplines (e.g., the Journal of Personality and Social Psychology and Psychological Science). Many of our faculty serve as co-Editors, Associate Editors, and on the editorial boards of these journals, actively shaping the field. The Marketing Area supports a thriving PhD program and fosters a collaborative atmosphere, with a state-of-the-art behavioral research lab, access to diverse field and secondary data through extensive industry partnerships, and a culture that values both rigorous scholarship and practical impact. About SMU and the Lee Kong Chian School of Business Singapore Management University (SMU) is a premier research university committed to rigorous, interdisciplinary work with real-world relevance. Located in the heart of Singapore’s downtown district, SMU offers a dynamic, globally oriented environment for both research and teaching. The Lee Kong Chian School of Business (LKCSB) has over 150 full-time faculty members and approximately 6,000 students. It consistently ranks among the top business schools worldwide, including in Financial Times and QS global rankings, and is accredited by both AACSB and EQUIS. In the newly released 2025 FT Business School Research Ranking, LKCSB is ranked 3rd in Asia and 23rd globally. We are proud to be the youngest business school in the global top 25. LKCSB offers globally competitive compensation, substantial research support (e.g., research funding, data, and RA support), and a low teaching load to facilitate high-quality scholarship. Living in Singapore: Singapore may measure just 24km by 44km, but its global impact and quality of life are immense. A vibrant city-state, it offers world-class amenities, excellent healthcare, and a safe environment, with one of the lowest crime rates globally. Its efficient public transport system (MRT, LRT, buses, taxis, and private-hire services), clean streets, and abundant greenery make it easy and pleasant to live and work in the city. Since independence, Singapore’s stable parliamentary democracy and strong, innovation-driven economy have transformed it into one of the world’s leading business and financial hubs. The city’s multicultural society—shaped by Chinese, Malay, Indian, and Eurasian communities—supports a rich tapestry of festivals, traditions, and cuisines. Residents enjoy diverse leisure options, from parks, nature trails, beaches, and sports facilities to theatres, museums, and galleries. Food enthusiasts can explore everything from acclaimed restaurants to local hawker centres, which are recognized by UNESCO as part of the world’s Intangible Cultural Heritage. Singapore’s advanced infrastructure and technology, including the Smart Nation initiative, underpin high-quality public services and a sustainable urban environment. With world-class connectivity through Changi International Airport, consistently voted among the best airports globally, Singapore offers an ideal base for both regional and international travel. Application procedure All applications should be submitted through our online portal : https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=250000C4&tz=GMT+08:00&tzname=Asia/Singapore Please include the following materials: Detailed curriculum vitae Three research samples For inquiries about the position (excluding application materials submissions), please contact Professor Thomas Allard, Marketing Area, Lee Kong Chian School of Business, Singapore Management University, at thomasallard@smu.edu.sg . #LI-DNI Qualifications Candidates must have an earned PhD in a field relevant to Marketing. Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : Marketing Job Posting : 13-Nov-2025, 6:31:08 AM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=2500007G": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Finance (2500007G)",
      "description": "Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Finance (2500007G) Go to the main content section. You are here Faculty Recruitment Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Finance (2500007G) Job Description Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Finance - ( 2500007G ) Description FULL-TIME FACULTY POSITIONS IN FINANCE LEE KONG CHIAN SCHOOL OF BUSINESS SINGAPORE MANAGEMENT UNIVERSITY DESCRIPTION Assistant, Associate, and Full Professors of Finance Singapore Management University (SMU) invites applications for finance tenure-track and tenured positions at all levels and in all areas of scholarship. Applications in digital, sustainable, entrepreneurial, and real estate finance are particularly encouraged. LKCSB has a particular focus on high-impact research. In the recent FT Research Impact ranking, LKCSB was ranked 2nd in Asia and 21st globally. Therefore, research with significant (potential) impact on industry or society is particularly welcome. FULL PROFESSOR/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR : Ph.D. and established track record of high-quality research with evidence of sustained scholarship and publications in top-tier finance journals. Candidates are expected to mentor junior faculty members in research and should have effective teaching at both the undergraduate and postgraduate levels. ASSISTANT PROFESSOR : Ph.D. in hand or very close to completion. Candidates are expected to demonstrate potential for high quality research. ABOUT LEE KONG CHIAN SCHOOL OF BUSINESS AND FINANCE GROUP AT SMU : Lee Kong Chian School of Business (LKCSB) at Singapore Management University is a dynamic business school with more than 5,000 students and over a hundred full-time faculty members. Triple-accredited by AACSB, EQUIS and AMBA, the school offers a full suite of undergraduate, master’s (including the MBA) and doctoral programmes. Faculty members in the Finance group at LKCSB received their doctorates from leading research universities and regularly publish in all top-tier finance journals. In the ASU finance research rankings, based on publications in the Journal of Finance , Journal of Financial Economics , Review of Financial Studies and Journal of Financial and Quantitative Analysis for the 2020-2024 period, SMU is ranked 37th worldwide. SMU subscribes to all major financial databases and provides generous research funds to support conference travel and other research activities. The finance group hosts an annual summer research camp, an active research seminar series, and visits by distinguished finance scholars. The finance group also has a PhD program with high quality students and good placements. For more information about the Finance group at SMU Lee Kong Chian School of Business, visit https://business.smu.edu.sg/business/disciplines/finance/welcome . For information about Singapore, visit https://www.edb.gov.sg/en/why-singapore/a-great-place-to-live.html . English is the primary language used for education, commerce, and daily life in Singapore. APPLICATION PROCEDURE AND DEADLINE : 15 November 2025 Applicants should submit their application package comprising a cover letter, CV, recent publications or working papers, teaching and research statements, and teaching evaluations via the following link : https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=2500007G&tz=GMT+08:00&tzname=Asia/Singapore In addition, three letters of recommendation should be sent via e-mail to financecv@smu.edu.sg . Please address your application to Prof Emiliano Pagnotta, Recruiting Chair and Associate Professor of Finance. Shortlisted applicants will be contacted for interviews. The first-round interviews will be conducted virtually via ZOOM before the 2026 AFA meeting. Singaporeans selected for tenure-track Assistant Professor positions may be considered for the Singapore Teaching and Academic Research Talent (START) Inauguration Grant.  Details on the grant application procedure may be found here: https://www.smu.edu.sg/moe-start/inauguration-grant #LI-DNI Qualifications Candidates must have an earned PhD in a field relevant to Finance. Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : Finance Job Posting : 02-Sep-2025, 12:49:54 AM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=25000074": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Operations Management",
      "description": "Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Operations Management (25000074) Go to the main content section. You are here Faculty Recruitment Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Operations Management (25000074) Job Description Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Operations Management - ( 25000074 ) Description TENURE-TRACK FACULTY POSITION IN OPERATIONS MANAGEMENT The Lee Kong Chian School of Business (LKCSB) at Singapore Management University (SMU) invites applications for multiple tenured/tenure-track faculty positions in Operations Management (OM) at all ranks. A Ph.D. (or near completion in the case of junior Assistant rank) in OM or a closely related field is required. While the positions are open for any candidate with research interests in broad domains of OM, those specializing in analytics (AI, machine learning), entrepreneurship, or sustainability are specifically encouraged to apply. LKCSB has a particular focus on high-impact research. In the recent FT Research Impact ranking, LKCSB was ranked 2nd in Asia and 21st  globally. Therefore, research with significant (potential) impact on industry or society is particularly welcome. LKCSB is a vibrant and culturally diverse business school, located in the heart of downtown Singapore, with approximately 5,500 students and over 130 full-time faculty members. The school offers a wide array of undergraduate and postgraduate programs, including Ph.D, MBA, EMBA, MSc, DBA, as well as executive education . The OM group at LKCSB consists of 24 faculty members with diverse research expertise with strong publication record. LKCSB provides internationally competitive remuneration, generous research support and conference funding. International faculty are offered housing and schooling subsidy as well as relocation assistance. The teaching load for pre-tenure faculty is 2 courses per academic year during their initial four-year contract, 3 courses per academic year during the second three-year contract (if renewed) and after tenure. Tenured faculty members with exceptional research performance are also eligible for reduced teaching loads. Applications must be submitted through the following link: Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Operations Management - (25000074) Applicants should include a full CV, up to three selected publications or working papers, and a cover letter. Applicants for pre-tenure positions should also include research and teaching statements. Shortlisted candidates will be asked to provide three reference letters (referees will be requested to send directly to the school). Candidates who start their application by 23:59 PM on October 6, 2025 (Singapore time, UTC/GMT +8) with an up-to-date CV will be considered for online interviews ahead of the INFORMS Annual Meeting. The deadline for completion of all submissions is 23:59 PM on November 3, 2025 (Singapore time, UTC/GMT +8). Late applications will be accepted, but may not receive full consideration. #LI-DNI Qualifications Candidates must have an earned PhD in a field relevant to Operations Management. Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : Operations Management Job Posting : 12-Aug-2025, 12:00:13 AM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=25000050": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Marketing",
      "description": "Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Marketing (25000050) Go to the main content section. You are here Faculty Recruitment Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Marketing (25000050) Job Description Full-Time Faculty, Tenure Track, Marketing - ( 25000050 ) Description FACULTY POSITIONS IN MARKETING (Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Tenure-Track/Tenured) The Marketing Area at the Lee Kong Chian School of Business is actively seeking applications for faculty positions at all levels in Marketing. We seek candidates with solid research and teaching records in all marketing areas: Quantitative Marketing, Marketing Strategy, and Consumer Behavior. The application deadline is June 30, 2025. About the Marketing Area Join a vibrant and rapidly growing Marketing Area at the Lee Kong Chian School of Business, recognized for its network of industry connections and high-impact research. Our faculty actively publishes in top journals, participates in editorial boards, and contributes significantly to the marketing PhD program. Experience a collegial and collaborative atmosphere, supported by a state-of-the-art behavioral research lab and extensive industry contacts. Find more information about the marketing group at: https://business.smu.edu.sg/disciplines/marketing/faculty . About SMU and the Lee Kong Chian School of Business Singapore Management University (SMU) prioritizes rigorous and high-impact research. With a state-of-the-art city campus in downtown Singapore, SMU offers a rewarding environment. The Lee Kong Chian School of Business, with over 120 full-time faculty and 3,000 students, ranks in the top 50 in FT and QS rankings globally. Accredited by AACSB and EQUIS, the School provides globally competitive remuneration, generous research support, and attractive teaching loads. Application procedure All applications should be submitted using the following link: https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=25000050&tz=GMT+08:00&tzname=Asia/Singapore Applications should include (1) a detailed CV, (2) a personal statement on research and teaching, (3) a job market paper or three research samples, (4) three reference letters and (5) a cover letter specifying the desired position/rank. All application materials should be uploaded as attachments under their profile via the system. (Reference letters can be uploaded as attachments under their profile via the system or sent directly to marketingcv@smu.edu.sg addressing the application to the Marketing Recruiting Committee. Inquiries about the position (not application material) can be sent to Associate Professor Sandeep Chandukala ( sandeepc@smu.edu.sg ). #LI-DNI Qualifications Candidates must have an earned PhD in a field relevant to Marketing. Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : Marketing Job Posting : 13-May-2025, 7:07:34 PM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
    },
