raduate, master’s (including the MBA) and doctoral programmes. Faculty members in the Finance group at LKCSB received their doctorates from leading research universities and regularly publish in all top-tier finance journals. In the ASU finance research rankings, based on publications in the Journal of Finance , Journal of Financial Economics , Review of Financial Studies and Journal of Financial and Quantitative Analysis for the 2019-2023 period, SMU is ranked 42nd worldwide. SMU subscribes to all major financial databases and provides generous research funds to support conference travel and other research activities. The finance group hosts an annual summer research camp, an active research seminar series, and visits by distinguished finance scholars. The finance group also has a PhD program with high quality students and good placements. For more information about the Finance group at SMU Lee Kong Chian School of Business, visit https://business.smu.edu.sg/business/disciplines/finance/welcome . For information about Singapore, visit https://www.edb.gov.sg/en/why-singapore/a-great-place-to-live.html . English is the primary language used for education, commerce, and daily life in Singapore. APPLICATION PROCEDURE AND DEADLINE : 10 November 2024 Applicants should submit their application package comprising a cover letter, CV, recent publications or working papers, teaching and research statements, and teaching evaluations via the following link : https://smucareers.taleo.net/careersection/smu_ext_ft/jobdetail.ftl?job=24000071&tz=GMT+08:00&tzname=Asia/Singapore In addition, three letters of recommendation should be sent via e-mail to financecv@smu.edu.sg . Please address your application to Dr. Jianfeng Hu, Recruiting Chair and Associate Professor of Finance. Shortlisted applicants will be contacted for interviews. The first-round interviews will be conducted virtually via ZOOM before the 2025 AFA meeting. Singaporeans selected for tenure-track Assistant Professor positions may be considered for the Singapore Teaching and Academic Research Talent (START) Inauguration Grant.  Details on the grant application procedure may be found here: https://www.smu.edu.sg/moe-start/inauguration-grant #LI-DNI Qualifications Candidates must have an earned PhD in a field relevant to Finance. Primary Location : Singapore Job : Full Time Organization : Finance Job Posting : 03-Sep-2024, 12:30:24 AM Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Instagram SoundCloud YouTube SMU Blog Where to Find Us Office of Human Resources Singapore Management University \n                        Administration Building \n                        81 Victoria Street \n                        Singapore 188065 © Copyright 2016 Singapore Management University. All Rights Reserved | Terms of Use Privacy Statement"
